{
  "format": "certen-finality-states/2",
  "notes": ["enums: field -> the CLOSED set of values of that field; a state whose field is outside it is a conformance failure.","conditional_required: when every key of `when` equals the state field, the `required` fields must also be present.","enums_defined_by: a reason field whose closed set is defined by the chain package that first raises the code (RB11-C..F); the conformance scan fails the moment such a code is raised without an enums.reason set.","Integer fields render as decimal strings for any width (state.go canonValue).","finality_header_chain_broken.reason is ONE closed set shared by every spine, each token with one meaning (RB11-INT1): hash (spines l1, l2) = the header at at_number (got_hash) is not the one its child commits to (want_hash) or the spine top is not the proven head; number (l1, l2) = the header numbers do not step by one; rlp (l1, l2) = the header bytes are not a decodable header; parent_hash_mismatch (adiri) = a block header's parentHash is not the hash of its predecessor; number_gap (adiri) = the block number skips. Published vector sets pin these tokens, so the sets that predate the union keep theirs.","finality_pending optional fields are the judged-at facts a builder attaches to a pending reason without the reason requiring them: eta (when the next level is expected), latest_finalized_slot / latest_finalized_exec_number / observed_head_slot (the L1 finalized head the answer was judged against, E1 and the awaiting_* reasons), captured_l1_block, l2_block, latest_captured_batch and finalized_exec_number. finality_upgrader_disabled carries env, value and effect; chain is its optional chain id when a per-chain switch is the cause (the env name already embeds it). RB12-DBFIX-FIX: reason is optional and has one value, config_invalid = the finality runtime was not started because a provider setting it parses was refused; then variable (the setting, equal to env), entry (its position among the setting's non-blank entries, -1: none) and class (what is wrong with the entry; never the value) are required and value is the word invalid. finality_ledger_extension_invalid.reason is the closed set of the LedgerReason constants in pkg/finality/ledger.go (RB11-C2).","Byte values (a []byte and every fixed byte array such as [4]byte or [32]byte) render as 0x-prefixed lower-case hex; the empty byte string is \"0x\" (state.go canonValue).","l1_capture_gap is ONE state with two producers, told apart by gap_state (RB12 Train 3): open, unavailable_proven and retention_expired = the capture has a durable gap record inside the leg window (the capture-gap branch; the window reader and the index path both consult the records) and the record shape (kind, from, to, ranges, blocks, epoch_l1_block, window_end_l1_block, archive_provider) is required; unrecorded = no record exists but the index shows captured channels of later L2 time past the capture retry window with no channel for the leg (the index inference) and the L2/L1 interval shape (l2_timestamp, l2_from, l2_to, from_l1, to_l1, partial_frames) is required. conditional_required enforces each shape; a state of either producer that lacks its shape does not conform."],
